Overlay patch 0014: iOS frame/tick cadence probe (port of reference 0008
into SpaghettiKart's engine; docs/probe.md). Per present records the wall
interval AND time inside DrawAndRunGraphicsCommands (eng_ms); per engine
iteration counts engine_fps (target 30); per process_game_tick counts
sim_tps (target 60 racing — MK64's gTickLogic=2; ~0 in menus, which don't
run race ticks). Every 10 s logs a SOH_PERF line (tag kept from the
reference so pull/parse tooling is shared) with thermal via the shell's
SohIos_ThermalState. __IOS__-only; desktop build unaffected.
Honest naming: wall and eng BOTH include in-present blocking — and, via
push_frame, the engine frame sits between StartAudioFrame/EndAudioFrame,
so an audio underrun surfaces as engine time. wall≈eng/N (N=interpolation
factor) healthy; wall>>expected with low eng = CPU outside the render call.

REV2 (VR R17-A item 1) — THE PER-WALK INTERPOLATION FACTOR, EXPORTED.
ProcessGfxCommands builds N matrix-replacement sets per GAME frame (N = 2 in
VR, where gMatchRefreshRate pins the interpolation target to the panel rate)
and RunCommands walks the display list once for each, at
FrameInterpolation_Interpolate(t) with t running 0.5, 1.0. Every OBJECT the
walk draws therefore advances in sub-frame steps — but the VR SEAT does not:
0044 composes its eye matrices from a kart pose exported once per GAME frame,
so relative to the seat a nearby kart alternates between "on time" and "half a
game frame ahead" on every present. That is the user's shaking ghost duplicate,
and the fix needs the walk's own t on the other side of the interface. This
revision publishes it and nothing else: `gSohVRWalkT` is set immediately before
each DrawAndRunGraphicsCommands, and the vector it comes from is filled where
the factors are computed. The non-__IOS__ build is byte-for-byte unchanged —
the interpolation call still takes the same expression it always did.

